<title>CANADA: CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</title>
<headline>CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vacant space in Canadian Prairie primary elevators fell to 31 percent in the week ended June 22 while railcar unloads fell short of target levels, Canadian Wheat Board said.</p>
<p>The 31 percent average vacancy in Prairie elevators was down from 35 percent on June 15, the Board said.</p>
<p>Manitoba had the most space available at 37 percent followed by Alberta at 34 percent and Saskatchewan had the least at 27 percent.</p>
<p>Vancouver unloaded 2,849 railcars versus the 3,300 target. Prince Rupert unloaded 1,122 railcars versus the 1,300 target.</p>
<p>Thunder Bay unloaded 3,644 railcars versus the 3,420 target.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
